1
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,580
When you watch TV,

2
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:12,940
turn on the room lights
and try sitting farther away.

3
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,160
it's as if someone is calling you,

4
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,700
a rainy afternoon after
the rain has stopped.

5
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,700
I walked while looking
back over my shoulder,

6
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,300
led along by the hand
of a capsule toy machine.

7
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:42,540
that strange feeling I had back then.

8
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:47,740
So on the arcade guide tiles,

9
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,520
I tried walking only on the black parts.

10
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:59,700
Everyone was a child once,

11
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,640
but everyone has forgotten.

12
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:09,160
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

13
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:14,720
Why don't you turn that corner over there?

14
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:19,920
You can meet everyone, everyone.

15
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,840
Over there is Kame-ari
surely there's a turtle there!

16
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:33,020
Everyone, come on over to our town!

17
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

18
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,600
It's three characters.

19
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,060
It's spring break.

20
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:42,020
Wow.

21
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:43,660
What are you doing?

22
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:45,040
We're doing finger-spelling.

23
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:47,140
The one where you write on
someone's back and they guess it.

24
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:49,680
Well, senpai never misses, you know.
He's 100 for 100.

25
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,700
Let me try too!

26
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:53,360
Can it be kanji too?

27
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,140
Well, just write it firmly.

28
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,360
Stand the horizontal stroke up,
then left, then right.

29
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,180
Got it? It's two characters.

30
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:02,500
This is kind of hard.

31
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,460
It's the character for "yuutsu."

32
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,140
Don't write a character
with that many strokes.

33
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:11,240
Even if you write it right in front of him,
I don't think Senpai will be able to read it.

34
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:12,260
I see.

35
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:13,220
Hey, you.

36
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,720
Then, Reiko, you try it next.

37
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,640
I'll give you the question.

38
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:18,960
Me?

39
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:22,840
Nakagawa,
tell me the hardest kanji in the world.

40
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:23,620
Well, let me think.

41
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:26,100
How about "lemon"?

42
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,600
Reiko knows her kanji well, after all.

43
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,260
No, how about "Baby, yoroshiku"?

44
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,280
I don't think you'll get it at all.

45
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,560
Decided! I'm writing it, Reiko.

46
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,600
I've got a bad feeling about this.

47
00:02:38,260 --> 00:02:38,680
Hey.

48
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:41,640
Stop tickling me, already.

49
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,380
I'm not tickling you.

50
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:46,540
Senpai, your touch is so lewd.

51
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:47,560
Exactly.

52
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:50,360
Fine. Then I'll write quickly.

53
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:51,360
Make it quick, okay.

54
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:54,166
Hahaha, "guguguu"...

55
00:02:54,216 --> 00:02:57,800
Stop it, Ryo-chan, stop, I said stop!

56
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,100
Ow that hurts!

57
00:02:59,100 --> 00:02:59,820
Sorry.

58
00:02:59,820 --> 00:03:03,040
Ryo-chan,
you should be the one guessing after all.

59
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:04,440
Don't use kanji.

60
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,800
If you guess it right,
I'll give you 100 yen.

61
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,640
Got it, Reiko?
It's 100 yen, so don't forget.

62
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:15,250
Um...

63
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:18,300
Ba, next is ga... ba, ba-ka.

64
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:19,800
It's about you.

65
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,660
Whoa, Chief!

66
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:23,760
Whoa, he really wrote "idiot"!

67
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:26,540
You should assert yourself like that.

68
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,300
Damn it, Chief...

69
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:33,360
Mobile Phone Panic!

70
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:40,640
Hello, this is

71
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:43,240
It's a cell phone, Chief.

72
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:45,080
It's not my ringtone.

73
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,940
It's not mine either.

74
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,340
Not this one, not this one either.

75
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:51,720
Not this one either,

76
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,460
this one's not it either.

77
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,400
How many do you even have?

78
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,940
So that means it's this one.

79
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:58,380
Even in a place like that?

80
00:03:58,380 --> 00:03:59,580
This one's not it either.

81
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:02,820
Whose cell phone is ringing, anyway?

82
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,500
Honestly, you two...

83
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:08,280
You can live without that kind of thing,
you know!

84
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,460
Yes, hello?

85
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:12,040
Yeah, got it.

86
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:14,840
So I just need to pick up
some yakiniku sauce, right?

87
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,700
Well, then.

88
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,100
Terai, you too?

89
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:24,360
No, my wife made me carry one because it's handy
when she asks me to pick up groceries on the way home.

90
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:31,340
See? Even Terai, the very picture of an ordinary commoner,
can't live without a cell phone anymore.

91
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:34,420
It's kind of nice when it rings, isn't it?

92
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:38,900
It makes you feel trusted,
or like you've become someone important.

93
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:43,560
We're entering an era where
everyone in Japan has a cell phone.

94
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,620
And yet you still cling to your prejudice.

95
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:50,200
Chief, you're a living fossil
left behind by the times.

96
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:52,000
What do you mean, a living fossil?

97
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,600
On trains and in public places,

98
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:57,940
I can't stand the manners of people
who use their phones without a care.

99
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:01,500
That's no reason to make cell
phones your sworn enemy, is it?

100
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:05,500
If you hate them so much, then go on living without
a cell phone for the rest of your life, Chief.

101
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,140
Fine by me.

102
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:09,700
I'm not troubled in the
least without that thing.

103
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,000
You said it, Chief.

104
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,900
I won't forget those words.

105
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,300
No need to take a step back.

106
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:17,440
Another stubborn standoff

107
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:19,860
It really is like a kids' squabble.

108
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:33,300
The chief got a cell phone?

109
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:36,940
After all that talk about
not needing a cell phone?

110
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:39,060
What changed your mind?

111
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:40,960
Well, it's nothing.

112
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:45,320
Hiromi said it was a prize from Hideo's golf competition,
so I took it.

113
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,540
I told her I didn't want it, though.

114
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:51,940
But Daisuke said with this,
you could hear Grandpa's voice anytime.

115
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:53,760
Ugh, how pathetic.

116
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:56,460
Changing your mind in just one day.

117
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,380
But that's not a bad thing.

118
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,440
That's right.

119
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,180
Well, when I looked into it,

120
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:05,380
there were all sorts of stories of people
getting out of tight spots thanks to their phones.

121
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:10,420
Like the person who went out alone to the mountains,
got hurt, and called for help on their phone.

122
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:13,760
And a person who got locked
inside their home sauna box

123
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:17,760
contacted the police and was rescued.

124
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:21,120
So that kind of thing happened too?

125
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:22,240
Mm.

126
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:24,740
I-it's ringing!

127
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:26,620
What was I supposed to do again?

128
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:30,680
Carrying a cell phone without even knowing how to use it,
honestly.

129
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:33,640
It's just a little door-scratch,
nothing more.

130
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:37,060
You press this part, Chief.

131
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:38,600
This one?

132
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,480
Yes, this is Ohara, go ahead.

133
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,640
It's not a police radio, you know.

134
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,520
Shut up!

135
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:47,600
Hello? Can you hear me?

136
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:50,100
Of course I can hear you, obviously!

137
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,400
Is that you, Daisuke?

138
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:52,480
What?

139
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,940
It's from your grandson, Daisuke.

140
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:59,700
One look at the chief's face tells us that.

141
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:01,220
Got it.

142
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,420
Well then, see you.

143
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:06,120
Ugh, he begged me for a toy, you know.

144
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:10,460
Could you all tell me
your phone numbers too?

145
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:15,000
If I register them as speed dial,
I can reach you with one button, right?

146
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,080
Yes, my number is...

147
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,180
Mine is...

148
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:21,220
It starts with 090...

149
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:25,620
Well, I'm off to the station now.

150
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:27,360
I'm counting on you for the rest.

151
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,300
Have a good trip.

152
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:31,980
He's finally gone.

153
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:33,680
Right then.

154
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:37,300
Ryo-chan, what's that?

155
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:40,760
Sensō-ji asked me to
make one for 20,000 yen.

156
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:44,320
I can't make it where the
chief can see me, right?

157
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:46,500
Right.

158
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:51,520
After all, it's a delicate task.

159
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,900
It's mine.

160
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:56,380
Hello? It's me.

161
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:57,560
This one's me too.

162
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,740
Chief.

163
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:01,700
You only just left.

164
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:04,140
I forgot. Listen, Ryotsu.

165
00:08:04,380 --> 00:08:06,940
Just because I'm not here,
don't go playing with radio-controlled cars

166
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:08,920
or building model kits!

167
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:11,400
W-we're not doing anything like that.

168
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:14,840
Work seriously. See you.

169
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:18,001
You startled me.

170
00:08:18,051 --> 00:08:21,200
You didn't have to call from so close by.

171
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:23,540
Right.

172
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:26,720
Now it's my turn.

173
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,180
Hello. It's Chief.

174
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:35,380
Reiko, did you remember to water the
planters in front of the police box?

175
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,800
Yes, I watered them this morning.

176
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,260
Good, that's all I needed. Thank you.

177
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:42,820
What?

178
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:45,560
He asked if you watered the planters.

179
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:50,380
This time it's my phone.
Yes, this is Nakagawa.

180
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:54,780
I forgot to mention,
I'll be back around 4 o'clock, so, see you.

181
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:57,980
He says he'll be back around 4 o'clock.

182
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:01,400
He keeps calling about
totally pointless things.

183
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:05,680
At this rate, he's no different from a chimpanzee
that just learned how to blow a trumpet.

184
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:07,700
Maybe it's him again.

185
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:08,720
Hello?

186
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,780
You idiot!

187
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,460
You were just badmouthing me, weren't you?

188
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:15,580
Don't yell so loudly, please.

189
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:18,100
Even without looking,
I can tell by instinct.

190
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,800
Listen,
you'd better behave yourselves, Ryotsun!

191
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:30,580
W-what, again?

192
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:32,360
Aren't you going to answer, Ryo-san?

193
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,580
It's probably the Chief again.

194
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:36,220
See?

195
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,220
I'm not answering it.

196
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:42,400
Ryo here!

197
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,160
Why don't you call in the morning!

198
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:47,760
You don't need to call.
I can hear you from right there!

199
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,840
Sigh.

200
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:53,280
Why isn't he calling me?

201
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:59,520
It's come in handy in all sorts of ways,
thanks to you.

202
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:01,800
Well then, give my regards to Hideo.

203
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:08,800
Dear, you have a landline,
so why bother calling on your cell phone?

204
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:11,440
Well, it's so convenient
that I just can't help it.

205
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:15,220
Calls on cell phones cost way more than landline calls,
you know.

206
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:18,380
Please don't lose it or drop it.

207
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:24,180
They say you can get charged a shocking
amount without even realizing it's been used.

208
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:27,760
I know,
I'm not going to make such a blunder.

209
00:10:29,860 --> 00:10:33,220
Right then, I'm off to Katsushika Police Station,
so I'm counting on you for the rest.

210
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:39,880
Finally gone. Now,
shall I pick up where I left off yesterday?

211
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:46,220
The chief went and forgot it, the idiot.

212
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:48,800
Payback for all the yelling
we put up with every day.

213
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:49,860
Just watch.

214
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:56,740
Is that Bagryu?

215
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,700
It's me. Where are you right now?

216
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,760
Doing drills in the North Pacific.

217
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:04,300
No, I don't really have any business.

218
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:08,440
I ended up talking on
the phone for a long time.

219
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:11,920
Speaking of which, that Hondara old man

220
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:14,320
said he was going to Australia for training.

221
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,600
Bookshelf old man, what's he up to now?

222
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,640
Intensive constitution training
for a thinking opponent.

223
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:26,340
No, I don't really have
any business, though.

224
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:31,580
Professor Tondemo, which country
has he gone crazy over this time?

225
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:34,340
He's heading to the North Pole by dog sled.

226
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:36,760
Well, I really don't have any business.

227
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,040
Hello, this is Ryo speaking.

228
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:44,460
Oh no, no.
I don't really have any business, though.

229
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:49,620
I should let the station know.

230
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:51,971
Strange... that's right.

231
00:11:52,021 --> 00:11:54,320
I left it at the police box.

232
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:58,320
This much use should be enough, right?

233
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:02,360
Wait till the chief hears the bill.
He'll be shocked!

234
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,600
Oops, yes.

235
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,820
Ryotsu-ka?

236
00:12:05,820 --> 00:12:07,160
Chief.

237
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:09,660
So he really left it there.

238
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:12,680
I'll be right back,
so keep an eye on my cell phone.

239
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,860
Watch?

240
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:17,500
Oh right, watch it. Got it?
Keep a close eye on it.

241
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:21,030
Yeah, yeah. Well then,

242
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:24,080
Should we finish up
before the chief gets back?

243
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:34,580
A pickpocket lives by his eyes, after all.

244
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:44,160
- Ryotsu!
- Whoa! Yes!

245
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:46,370
Where's my cell phone?

246
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:49,940
It's on the desk over there.

247
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:51,614
There? Where?

248
00:12:51,664 --> 00:12:54,560
No, where? On the Chief's desk.

249
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:58,740
- It's not here.
- That's strange. I'm sure I left it right on top of this.

250
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:00,760
Ryotsu!

251
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:04,450
You! What were you doing during work hours!?

252
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:06,880
Well, that's, you see...

253
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:11,210
Never mind
"you see"! Where did you put my cell phone!?

254
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,480
I was mistaken.

255
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,700
It was never here to begin with.

256
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,960
You answered the phone just now, didn't you?

257
00:13:18,960 --> 00:13:20,080
Don't try to dodge the question.

258
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,120
You were so absorbed in making this thing,

259
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:24,980
you didn't notice someone took it, did you?

260
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:26,400
Listen, Ryotsu.

261
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:29,060
Find my cell phone no matter what.

262
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:30,900
Whatever gets charged in the meantime,

263
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:33,480
you'll be paying for it out of your salary.

264
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:34,680
No way.

265
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:36,180
Yeah.

266
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:55,040
Thank you for watching.

267
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,480
Yes, yes.

268
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:24,500
Yes, this is Ohara speaking.

269
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:26,620
No, Chief.

270
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:30,300
You said you'd leave your wife.

271
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:33,880
Hey, who are you? Hello?

272
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,740
Besides,
it's the Chief's child-rearing, after all.

273
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:37,620
Hello?

274
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,140
Hello?

275
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:41,680
Hello?

276
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:50,400
Is that you, Ohara-kun?

277
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:51,920
Hello?

278
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:53,680
Marry me.

279
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:58,340
I've loved you since
the moment we first met.

280
00:14:58,340 --> 00:14:59,240
I love you.

281
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:01,980
Suddenly saying something like that...

282
00:15:01,980 --> 00:15:05,180
I have a wife, children, and a cat.

283
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:06,900
That doesn't matter.

284
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,860
How manly.

285
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:13,080
No, no, no! We're both men!

286
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:16,580
If you don't marry me, I'll die!

287
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:17,620
What!?

288
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:23,640
I can't possibly live without you.
You're my everything.

289
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:29,680
Ohara-kun!
Don't do anything rash! Ohara-kun!

290
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,540
It's mine.

291
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:43,220
It's my cell phone.

292
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:45,880
Stop being moved and answer it already!

293
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,820
Hello, hello?

294
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:51,880
This is the familiar old junk-mail exchange service,
as always.

295
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:53,100
What is this?

296
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,320
Can you hear me, Kaseoi?

297
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,260
I don't know who you are, but

298
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:00,620
I want it back.

299
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:03,480
Damn, they hung up.

300
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:09,080
Yes, this is the Kōen-mae police box.

301
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:11,420
It's you.

302
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:13,400
What?

303
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,860
What on earth is going on?

304
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,420
Who was that woman just now?

305
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:22,040
You, sir, are sleeping with
someone your own daughter's age.

306
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:24,100
W-what are you talking about?

307
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,560
I have no idea.

308
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:32,130
Hello, this is Kōen-mae Police Box.

309
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:34,520
Chief, it's a call from the station chief.

310
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:36,620
Hey, you!

311
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:40,960
Hello, this is Ohara speaking.
What did you say?

312
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:44,133
Don't do anything rash. No, wait,

313
00:16:44,183 --> 00:16:47,180
I-I'm flattered by your feelings,
but, well...

314
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,160
Y-yes...

315
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:55,340
Yes it's been a while.
Please hold on a moment.

316
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:58,180
Chief, it's a call from Hiromi.

317
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,620
Excuse me for a moment.

318
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:04,840
What is it, Hiromi?

319
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:08,060
What? I'm being transferred to Alaska?

320
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:11,740
You got a call?
That must be someone's prank.

321
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:14,740
It's not that I dislike you at all,

322
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:17,620
but marrying you as a man

323
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:18,680
Marriage?

324
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:21,880
Hello? Hey, what's this about marriage?

325
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,720
What's going on? Hey, you!

326
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,900
No, wait,
this is a different matter entirely.

327
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:31,620
Let's keep being good friends from now on,
shall we?

328
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:33,700
No, no, I mean, a symbol...

329
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,480
A symbol?

330
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:36,100
You're marrying a symbol?

331
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:36,460
So...

332
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:38,280
There's only circumstantial evidence, right?

333
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:38,860
So that's fine.

334
00:17:38,860 --> 00:17:39,820
Aki!

335
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:43,660
Listen, Ryotsu.

336
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:45,980
No matter what you do, whatever happens,

337
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:47,640
you get my cell phone back.

338
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,720
If you fail, you're fired, got it?

339
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:52,540
Search for it?
How the hell am I supposed to do that?

340
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:53,900
Damn it.

341
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:57,380
It's the Chief again.

342
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:00,060
It's from the missing cell phone.

343
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:01,420
Hello?

344
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:04,720
What is this?

345
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:08,480
And here it comes again!
Lucky start on the 70 series!

346
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,320
Jan-jan-bari-bari, jan-jan-bari-bari!

347
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:13,000
Everyone, let's go all out with full energy!

348
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,480
Next up, the 18 series!

349
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:16,720
This van is from the pachinko
hall in front of the station.

350
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,740
Is the Chief's phone
in front of the station?

351
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:26,920
Anyone talking on their cell phone

352
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,720
Seriously, for real.

353
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:36,280
Everyone's got one.

354
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:41,020
Hey, who the hell are you?
Give me back my phone!

355
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,280
If you can hear me, at least answer!

356
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:52,460
Ishiyaki mo, yaki mo...

357
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:55,740
Roasted sweet potatoes?

358
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:58,520
At this time of year and this hour,
it's over there.

359
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:08,420
Hey, didn't someone carrying a
cell phone just pass through here?

360
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:09,080
Cell phone?

361
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:11,380
No, nobody passed through.

362
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:14,160
That can't be right.
Someone must have passed through.

363
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,980
If you're lying, I'll arrest you.

364
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:21,020
This sound...

365
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,880
It's the road construction
noise from 3-chome.

366
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:28,540
Wait there, don't move.

367
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:38,540
Damn, he hung up!

368
00:19:40,940 --> 00:19:42,800
It should be somewhere near here.

369
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,760
Argh, I can't find it.

370
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:49,540
In that case, I'll call it myself.

371
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:52,640
There must be someone here!

372
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,900
Hey! Where are you hiding?!

373
00:19:58,120 --> 00:19:59,620
Come out quietly!

374
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:03,920
Hand it over!

375
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:06,300
My bag!

376
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:07,540
Thief!

377
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:08,640
What?

378
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:13,120
Where's the thief?

379
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:19,940
You bastard!

380
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:20,120
Whoa!

381
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,840
Ugh! P-police!

382
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:22,920
I'm not letting you get away!

383
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:23,860
Ugh!

384
00:20:24,080 --> 00:20:25,460
You, Kamenshiro!

385
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:26,620
Ow-ow-ow-ow-ow!

386
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:30,120
Thank you very much.

387
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:33,220
Great work, Officer.

388
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:34,460
Seriously, that's amazing.

389
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:36,820
No, I mean this, the... ceremony thing.

390
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:40,245
I guess it's from my steady,
everyday patrols,

391
00:20:40,295 --> 00:20:42,560
thanks to the chief's cell
phone getting stolen...

392
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:42,900
Ugh!

393
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:44,060
Whoa!

394
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:45,620
So it's you!

395
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:47,940
Ugh!

396
00:20:49,940 --> 00:20:50,420
Can't be helped.

397
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:55,640
Take him in for me,
at the scene, in my place.

398
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,200
I'm counting on you, auntie.

399
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:02,740
Get back here!

400
00:21:09,820 --> 00:21:11,260
Stop!

401
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,100
Stop!

402
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:25,720
I won't let you get away!

403
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:31,080
Damn you!

404
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,400
Get off me!

405
00:21:48,560 --> 00:21:49,900
You're not getting away!

406
00:21:50,140 --> 00:21:51,040
What!?

407
00:21:54,920 --> 00:22:18,040
Grrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrr

408
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:18,920
Making me chase you all over the place!

409
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:24,000
Got it back, somehow.

410
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:28,440
That damn dog.

411
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:29,660
Grabbing everything

412
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:30,680
and carrying it off in its mouth!

413
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:32,100
Whatever.

414
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:34,660
Anyway, I got the chief's cell phone back.

415
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:39,220
Yes.

416
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:40,780
Senpai.

417
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:41,680
It's Ryotsu.

418
00:22:41,680 --> 00:22:42,780
Where are you?

419
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:44,820
Did you get my cell phone back?

420
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:45,880
Senpai.

421
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:47,060
Where are you now?

422
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:49,800
Behind the police box?

423
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:54,260
There's a lot missing from the police box

424
00:22:54,260 --> 00:22:56,740
My electronic organizer.

425
00:22:56,740 --> 00:22:58,960
One of my shoes, too.

426
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:02,400
There's also the teacup
the chief loved so much.

427
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:04,840
It was all the dog's doing.

428
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:09,380
But thanks to my heroic efforts,
it's all been resolved safely.

429
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:11,120
What's this?

430
00:23:14,840 --> 00:23:16,860
Look, I hate to say this, but

431
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:19,960
show me your police notebook.

432
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:22,440
Not your teeth, just show me it already.

433
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,740
Right here, see?

434
00:23:27,100 --> 00:23:30,540
Ryotsu!

435
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:34,460
Idiot, yours is right here!

436
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:40,120
Come to think of it, I haven't been
able to find it for about a month now.

437
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,986
As a police officer,

438
00:23:42,036 --> 00:23:45,400
how dare you lose your important
notebook and keep quiet about it!

439
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:47,980
But isn't it that dog's fault?

440
00:23:47,980 --> 00:23:51,980
Even so,
you've been covering it up with this toy?

441
00:23:51,980 --> 00:23:52,660
But...

442
00:23:52,660 --> 00:23:55,900
No "buts"! You're getting no pay this month!

443
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:56,760
No way...

444
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:05,580
Kicked the alarm clock,
stubbed my pinky toe, ow ow ow

445
00:24:05,580 --> 00:24:13,800
Somehow draw my eyebrows, then dance,
dance, dance all the way to the station

446
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:19,560
On the train,
back on the homeward road, a quick nap

447
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:25,880
Another tough week, what hard work,
your unreasonable demands are quite fair

448
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:33,320
Baguette in hand, playing it cool,
but it's a beef bowl with extra sauce

449
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:40,260
Endless overtime frustration,
cleared away with more frustration

450
00:25:04,020 --> 00:25:09,340
I love me, every day is a no-brainer

451
00:25:09,340 --> 00:25:13,060
Hearts flying, Monday

452
00:25:13,060 --> 00:25:16,720
Anren, anren, no burg

453
00:25:20,740 --> 00:25:22,560
Chief, president

454
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:24,620
Chief, me, Kankichi Ryotsu

455
00:25:24,620 --> 00:25:27,720
I'll be serving as your
tour conductor this time

456
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:30,040
Hot springs, gourmet food,
and beautiful women

457
00:25:30,040 --> 00:25:33,140
I guarantee a trip you'll
be completely satisfied with

458
00:25:34,020 --> 00:25:37,580
Next time: Tabimakase Onsen Tour.
See you then!

